Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Induction and Recursion", "BookChapterTitle",
 CounterAssignments->{{"ChapterNumber", 5}}],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Introduction", "Section"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In this chapter we describe how ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " can be used to help you make conjectures and prove them with mathematical \
induction and strong induction. We will also look at several examples of \
using ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to explore recursive definitions and to implement recursive algorithms. \
Recursion is an important tool in any computer programming language, and ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is no exception. We conclude with an example of proving program \
correctness of a ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " function. "
}], "Text"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["5.1 Mathematical Induction", "Section",
 CellTags->"Section1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In this section we will demonstrate how to use ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " both to discover propositions and to aid in the use of mathematical \
induction to verify them. We begin with two examples of how to use ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to discover and prove summation formulas. We then consider a question of \
divisibility. "
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Summation Example 1", "Subsection",
 CellTags->"Section1a"],

Cell["\<\
As our first example, we will explore a formula that you've already seen: \
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    UnderoverscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"i", "=", "1"}], "TI"], "n",
     LimitsPositioning->False], "i"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"1", "+", "2", "+", "3", "+", "\[CenterEllipsis]", "+", "n"}], 
    "=", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"n", "(", 
      RowBox[{"n", "+", "1"}], ")"}], "2"]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "Equation"],

Cell["\<\
This formula is the subject of Example 1 in Section 5.1 of the text. Here, we \
will proceed as if we did not already know the formula. \
\>", "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Listing and Graphing to Find the Formula", "Subsubsection"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Our first step is to discover the formula. To do this, we will have ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " compute the sums for a variety of values of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["n", TraditionalForm]]],
 ", using the ",
 StyleBox[ButtonBox["Sum",
  BaseStyle->"Link",
  ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Sum"], "FunctionLink"],
 " function. "
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 StyleBox[ButtonBox["Sum",
  BaseStyle->"Link",
  ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Sum"], "FunctionLink"],
 " function has essentially the same syntax as ",
 StyleBox[ButtonBox["Table",
  BaseStyle->"Link",
  ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Table"], "FunctionLink"],
 ". The first argument is an expression representing the values to be added \
in terms of a variable. The second argument is a list indicating the values \
of the variable over which the sum should be computed. Refer to Section 2.4 \
for a  description of the behavior of the second argument. A table \
summarizing the main possibilities is shown below."
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell[BoxData[
     RowBox[{"{", 
      StyleBox["i", "CodeVar"], ",", 
      StyleBox[
       SubscriptBox["i", "max"], "CodeVar"], "}"}]], "myCode"], Cell[TextData[{
     "sum from ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
       RowBox[{"i", "=", "1"}], TraditionalForm]]],
     " to ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
       SubscriptBox["i", "max"], TraditionalForm]]]
    }]]},
   {Cell[BoxData[
     RowBox[{"{", 
      StyleBox["i", "CodeVar"], ",", 
      StyleBox[
       SubscriptBox["i", "min"], "CodeVar"], ",", 
      StyleBox[
       SubscriptBox["i", "max"], "CodeVar"], "}"}]], "myCode"], 
    RowBox[{"sum", " ", "from", " ", Cell[TextData[{
      Cell[BoxData[
       FormBox[
        RowBox[{"i", "=", 
         SubscriptBox["i", "min"]}], TraditionalForm]]],
      " to ",
      Cell[BoxData[
       FormBox[
        SubscriptBox["i", "max"], TraditionalForm]]]
     }]]}]},
   {Cell[BoxData[
     RowBox[{"{", 
      StyleBox["i", "CodeVar"], ",", 
      StyleBox[
       SubscriptBox["i", "min"], "CodeVar"], ",", 
      StyleBox[
       SubscriptBox["i", "max"], "CodeVar"], ",", 
      StyleBox["step", "CodeVar"], "}"}]], "myCode"], 
    RowBox[{"sum", " ", "from", " ", Cell[TextData[{
      Cell[BoxData[
       FormBox[
        RowBox[{"i", "=", 
         SubscriptBox["i", "min"]}], TraditionalForm]]],
      " to ",
      Cell[BoxData[
       FormBox[
        SubscriptBox["i", "max"], TraditionalForm]]],
      " by ",
      Cell[BoxData[
       FormBox["step", TraditionalForm]]]
     }]]}]},
   {Cell[BoxData[
     RowBox[{"{", 
      StyleBox["i", "CodeVar"], ",", 
      StyleBox["list", "CodeVar"], "}"}]], "myCode"], 
    RowBox[{
    "sum", " ", "over", " ", Cell["i\[Element]list"], Cell[TextData[StyleBox[
     "", "Input"]]]}]}
  },
  GridBoxDividers->{
   "Columns" -> {{True}}, "ColumnsIndexed" -> {}, "Rows" -> {{True}}, 
    "RowsIndexed" -> {}}]],
 FontFamily->"Times"]], "Text",
 TextAlignment->Center],

Cell["\<\
In our situation, we want to add the first several positive integers. For \
example, the sum of the first ten positive integers is \
\>", "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Sum", "[", 
  RowBox[{"i", ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"i", ",", "10"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData["55"], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To discover the formula for the sum of the first ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["n", TraditionalForm]]],
 " positive integers, we need several specific examples to analyze. To \
calculate a lot of examples at once, we will embed the ",
 StyleBox[ButtonBox["Sum",
  BaseStyle->"Link",
  ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Sum"], "FunctionLink"],
 " function inside of a ",
 StyleBox[ButtonBox["Table",
  BaseStyle->"Link",
  ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Table"], "FunctionLink"],
 ", with the maximum value of the summation as the table variable. This will \
produce the list of the sums of the first ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["n", TraditionalForm]]],
 " positive integers for different values of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["n", TraditionalForm]]],
 "."
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Sum", "[", 
    RowBox[{"i", ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"i", ",", "n"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"n", ",", "50"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
  "1", ",", "3", ",", "6", ",", "10", ",", "15", ",", "21", ",", "28", ",", 
   "36", ",", "45", ",", "55", ",", "66", ",", "78", ",", "91", ",", "105", 
   ",", "120", ",", "136", ",", "153", ",", "171", ",", "190", ",", "210", 
   ",", "231", ",", "253", ",", "276", ",", "300", ",", "325", ",", "351", 
   ",", "378", ",", "406", ",", "435", ",", "465", ",", "496", ",", "528", 
   ",", "561", ",", "595", ",", "630", ",", "666", ",", "703", ",", "741", 
   ",", "780", ",", "820", ",", "861", ",", "903", ",", "946", ",", "990", 
   ",", "1035", ",", "1081", ",", "1128", ",", "1176", ",", "1225", ",", 
   "1275"}], "}"}]], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Remember that we're working as if we do not already know the answer. Just \
looking at the data, you might notice a pattern, but if not, it's sometimes \
helpful to pair the value of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["n", TraditionalForm]]],
 " with the result. To do this, we only need to modify the ",
 StyleBox[ButtonBox["Table",
  BaseStyle->"Link",
  ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Table"], "FunctionLink"],
 " function so that the first argument is the list whose first element is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["n", TraditionalForm]]],
 " and whose second is the ",
 StyleBox[ButtonBox["Sum",
  BaseStyle->"Link",
  ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Sum"], "FunctionLink"],
 " function. "
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"n", ",", 
     RowBox[{"Sum", "[", 
      RowBox[{"i", ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"i", ",", "n"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"n", ",", "50"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input"],

